      "content": "For traditionalists, the secular approach is fundamentally flawed because it wrongly divorces morality from its objective, transcendent source. Their critique isn't just that it's unwise, but that it's logically impossible to build a stable moral framework without grounding it in Natural Law or divine decree. From their perspective, modernism fails because it jettisons the presupposition that human life has an inherent, objective purpose given by a higher power. Therefore, their defense of traditionalism is presented as the only logically coherent anchor against moral chaos.",
